= Object <bylaw>
The object of the Society shall be to:
- Serve, represent, and promote undergraduate students in the Faculty of
  Mathematics at the University of Waterloo by providing services to students;
- Encourage and coordinate student participation in athletic, cultural, social,
  academic, and recreational activities;
- Encourage cooperation and communication between students;
- Increase awareness of the Faculty and of mathematics in general to the outside
  community by representing students to the Faculty and to the University; and
- Provide students with the means to help them accomplish their goals both
  within and without the University.
